          "paragraphId": "P2",
          "quote": "they think that they had better agree among themselves to have neither; hence there arise laws and mutual covenants"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The student interprets the agreement in the text as a strategy to facilitate committing injustice, whereas the source text presents the agreement as a mutual compromise to avoid both the doing and suffering of injustice.",
      "uncertainty": "The student may be interpreting 'the agreement' as a tool for collective or selective action not present in the text, or misreading the purpose of 'laws and mutual covenants'.",
